{"type":"data","nodes":[null,{"type":"data","data":[{"tree":1},[2,20],{"slug":3,"title":4,"pages":5},"start","Start",[6,14],{"siteId":7,"section":3,"slug":8,"path":9,"title":10,"description":11,"order":12,"verified":13},"watch","install","/content/watch/docs/start/install.md","Install","Prebuilt binaries, the Docker image, building from Zig source, or installing through NullHub.",1,"v2026.5.29",{"siteId":7,"section":3,"slug":15,"path":16,"title":17,"description":18,"order":19,"verified":13},"quickstart","/content/watch/docs/start/quickstart.md","Quickstart","Seed demo data, start the API, and inspect your first runs in five minutes.",2,{"slug":21,"title":22,"pages":23},"reference","Reference",[24,29],{"siteId":7,"section":21,"slug":25,"path":26,"title":27,"description":28,"order":12,"verified":13},"api","/content/watch/docs/reference/api.md","HTTP API","Endpoints, data model, query parameters and token auth for the NullWatch JSON API.",{"siteId":7,"section":21,"slug":30,"path":31,"title":32,"description":33,"order":19,"verified":13},"cli","/content/watch/docs/reference/cli.md","CLI","Every NullWatch command — serve, query, ingest, demo-seed — with flags and examples."],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"doc":1,"raw":10,"dateModified":35,"sectionTitle":36,"prev":37,"next":43},{"siteId":2,"section":3,"slug":4,"path":5,"title":6,"description":7,"order":8,"verified":9,"body":10,"html":11,"toc":12},"watch","reference","cli","/content/watch/docs/reference/cli.md","CLI","Every NullWatch command — serve, query, ingest, demo-seed — with flags and examples.",2,"v2026.5.29","\nThe CLI covers local automation and scripting: it starts the server, queries stored data directly (no server required), and ingests spans and evals by hand. Examples use `zig build run --` as the README does; with a prebuilt binary, call it directly instead.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> Pre-1.0: config and CLI may change between releases.\n\n## Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| `serve` | Run the JSON HTTP API server (the default when no arguments are given) |\n| `summary` | Print the aggregate summary |\n| `runs` | List runs |\n| `run \u003Crun-id>` | Inspect one run in detail (exits `1` if the run does not exist) |\n| `spans` | List spans |\n| `evals` | List evals |\n| `ingest-span --json '\u003Cspan>'` | Ingest one span |\n| `ingest-eval --json '\u003Ceval>'` | Ingest one eval |\n| `demo-seed` | Seed deterministic local demo data |\n| `version` (or `--version`) | Print the embedded version string |\n| `help` (or `--help`, `-h`) | Print usage |\n| `--export-manifest` | Print a NullHub manifest (must be the first argument) |\n| `--from-json '\u003Cconfig>'` | Bootstrap config from wizard answers (must be the first argument) |\n\n## Shared flags\n\nEvery subcommand accepts three runtime flags:\n\n| Flag | Default | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `--data-dir PATH` | `~/.nullwatch/data` | Where the JSONL store lives |\n| `--config PATH` | `~/.nullwatch/config.json` | Alternate config file |\n| `--token TOKEN` | none | API token, overriding `api_token` from the config |\n\n## serve\n\n```bash\nzig build run -- serve\n```\n\nDefaults to `127.0.0.1:7710`. To bind elsewhere:\n\n```bash\nzig build run -- serve --host 0.0.0.0 --port 7710\n```\n\n| Flag | Default | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `--host` | `127.0.0.1` | Interface to bind |\n| `--port` | `7710` | Port to listen on |\n\n`--host` and `--port` exist only on `serve`; the [shared flags](#shared-flags) work here too.\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> Binding `0.0.0.0` exposes the API beyond your machine. Set `api_token` in the config first — see [HTTP API](/docs/reference/api/).\n\n## Query commands\n\nAll query commands read the local JSONL store under `~/.nullwatch/data`; the server does not need to be running.\n\n```bash\nzig build run -- summary\nzig build run -- runs --verdict pass --limit 20\nzig build run -- spans --source nullclaw --tool-name shell --limit 50\nzig build run -- evals --dataset prod-shadow --verdict fail\nzig build run -- run run-123\n```\n\n| Command | Flags |\n| --- | --- |\n| `runs` | `--run-id`, `--source`, `--operation`, `--status`, `--model`, `--tool-name`, `--verdict`, `--dataset`, `--limit` |\n| `spans` | `--run-id`, `--trace-id`, `--source`, `--operation`, `--status`, `--model`, `--tool-name`, `--task-id`, `--session-id`, `--agent-id`, `--limit` |\n| `evals` | `--run-id`, `--verdict`, `--eval-key`, `--scorer`, `--dataset`, `--limit` |\n\n## Ingest commands\n\nBoth take a single JSON document via `--json`. Field meanings are in the [data model](/docs/reference/api/).\n\n```bash\nzig build run -- ingest-span --json '{\n  \"run_id\": \"run-123\",\n  \"trace_id\": \"trace-123\",\n  \"span_id\": \"span-1\",\n  \"source\": \"nullclaw\",\n  \"operation\": \"model.call\",\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"started_at_ms\": 1710000000000,\n  \"ended_at_ms\": 1710000000320,\n  \"model\": \"gpt-5\",\n  \"prompt_version\": \"reply-v3\",\n  \"input_tokens\": 420,\n  \"output_tokens\": 96,\n  \"cost_usd\": 0.018\n}'\n```\n\n```bash\nzig build run -- ingest-eval --json '{\n  \"run_id\": \"run-123\",\n  \"eval_key\": \"helpfulness\",\n  \"scorer\": \"llm-judge\",\n  \"score\": 0.94,\n  \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n  \"dataset\": \"prod-shadow\"\n}'\n```\n\n## demo-seed\n\n```bash\nzig build run -- demo-seed\n```\n\nCreates a deterministic demo dataset of 3 runs (11 spans, 3 evals): a passing code-review run, a failed tool-call run, and a handoff/retry run with checkpoint context. No API keys, no hosted services, no agent workload. Seeding is idempotent — a second run skips all three existing run ids (`runs_skipped: 3`) and creates nothing. Useful for demos, manual testing, and trying the [NullHub](https://hub.nullmenu.ai/) Observability page against real-shaped data:\n\n```bash\nzig build run -- demo-seed\nzig build run -- runs --limit 20\nzig build run -- run demo-tool-failure\n```\n\n## NullHub integration flags\n\nNullWatch stays headless; these two flags let NullHub own installation and setup. Each must be the first argument — they are commands, not modifiers. `--export-manifest` prints a JSON manifest with platform assets, ports and a 4-step setup-wizard schema; `--from-json` writes `~/.nullwatch/config.json` from the wizard's answers:\n\n```bash\n# print the nullhub manifest describing this component\nzig build run -- --export-manifest\n\n# write config from wizard answers\nzig build run -- --from-json '{\"home\":\"~/.nullwatch\",\"port\":7710,\"data_dir\":\"data\"}'\n```\n\nThe `--from-json` payload also accepts `host` and `api_token`, matching the config file fields.\n\n## Environment\n\n| Variable | Used by | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `NULLWATCH_HOME` | nullwatch | Alternate home directory instead of `~/.nullwatch`; when unset, `HOME` is used (`USERPROFILE` on Windows) |\n| `NULLWATCH_URL` | NullHub | Where NullHub finds a running NullWatch, e.g. `http://127.0.0.1:7710` |\n","\u003Cp>The CLI covers local automation and scripting: it starts the server, queries stored data directly (no server required), and ingests spans and evals by hand. Examples use \u003Ccode>zig build run --\u003C/code> as the README does; with a prebuilt binary, call it directly instead.\u003C/p>\n\u003Caside class=\"callout callout--note\">\u003Cdiv class=\"callout-title\">Note\u003C/div>\u003Cp>Pre-1.0: config and CLI may change between releases.\u003C/p>\n\u003C/aside>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"commands\" aria-labelledby=\"heading-label-commands\">\u003Cspan id=\"heading-label-commands\">Commands\u003C/span>\u003Ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#commands\" aria-label=\"Permalink to Commands\" data-pagefind-ignore>\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\">#\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Data table: Command, Purpose\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ctable>\n\u003Cthead>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Cth>Command\u003C/th>\n\u003Cth>Purpose\u003C/th>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003C/thead>\n\u003Ctbody>\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>serve\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Run the JSON HTTP API server (the default when no arguments are given)\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>summary\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Print the aggregate summary\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>runs\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>List runs\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>run &lt;run-id&gt;\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Inspect one run in detail (exits \u003Ccode>1\u003C/code> if the run does not exist)\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>spans\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>List spans\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>evals\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>List evals\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>ingest-span --json &#39;&lt;span&gt;&#39;\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Ingest one span\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>ingest-eval --json &#39;&lt;eval&gt;&#39;\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Ingest one eval\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>demo-seed\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Seed deterministic local demo data\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>version\u003C/code> (or \u003Ccode>--version\u003C/code>)\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Print the embedded version string\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>help\u003C/code> (or \u003Ccode>--help\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>-h\u003C/code>)\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Print usage\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>--export-manifest\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Print a NullHub manifest (must be the first argument)\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>--from-json &#39;&lt;config&gt;&#39;\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Bootstrap config from wizard answers (must be the first argument)\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003C/tbody>\n\u003C/table>\n\u003C/div>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"shared-flags\" aria-labelledby=\"heading-label-shared-flags\">\u003Cspan id=\"heading-label-shared-flags\">Shared flags\u003C/span>\u003Ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#shared-flags\" aria-label=\"Permalink to Shared flags\" data-pagefind-ignore>\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\">#\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>Every subcommand accepts three runtime flags:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Data table: Flag, Default, Meaning\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ctable>\n\u003Cthead>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Cth>Flag\u003C/th>\n\u003Cth>Default\u003C/th>\n\u003Cth>Meaning\u003C/th>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003C/thead>\n\u003Ctbody>\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>--data-dir PATH\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>~/.nullwatch/data\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Where the JSONL store lives\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>--config PATH\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>~/.nullwatch/config.json\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Alternate config file\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>--token TOKEN\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>none\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>API token, overriding \u003Ccode>api_token\u003C/code> from the config\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003C/tbody>\n\u003C/table>\n\u003C/div>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"serve\" aria-labelledby=\"heading-label-serve\">\u003Cspan id=\"heading-label-serve\">serve\u003C/span>\u003Ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#serve\" aria-label=\"Permalink to serve\" data-pagefind-ignore>\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\">#\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cfigure class=\"code-figure\" data-lang=\"bash\">\u003Cpre class=\"shiki null-kitchen\" style=\"background-color:#0a0806;color:#d9d1c3\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#ECE5D8\">zig\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> build\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> serve\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\u003Cbutton class=\"code-copy\" type=\"button\" data-code data-pagefind-ignore aria-live=\"polite\">copy\u003C/button>\u003C/figure>\n\u003Cp>Defaults to \u003Ccode>127.0.0.1:7710\u003C/code>. To bind elsewhere:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cfigure class=\"code-figure\" data-lang=\"bash\">\u003Cpre class=\"shiki null-kitchen\" style=\"background-color:#0a0806;color:#d9d1c3\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#ECE5D8\">zig\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> build\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> serve\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --host\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#D9A441\"> 0.0.0.0\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --port\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#D9A441\"> 7710\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\u003Cbutton class=\"code-copy\" type=\"button\" data-code data-pagefind-ignore aria-live=\"polite\">copy\u003C/button>\u003C/figure>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Data table: Flag, Default, Meaning\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ctable>\n\u003Cthead>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Cth>Flag\u003C/th>\n\u003Cth>Default\u003C/th>\n\u003Cth>Meaning\u003C/th>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003C/thead>\n\u003Ctbody>\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>--host\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>127.0.0.1\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Interface to bind\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>--port\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>7710\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Port to listen on\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003C/tbody>\n\u003C/table>\n\u003C/div>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>--host\u003C/code> and \u003Ccode>--port\u003C/code> exist only on \u003Ccode>serve\u003C/code>; the \u003Ca href=\"#shared-flags\">shared flags\u003C/a> work here too.\u003C/p>\n\u003Caside class=\"callout callout--warning\">\u003Cdiv class=\"callout-title\">Warning\u003C/div>\u003Cp>Binding \u003Ccode>0.0.0.0\u003C/code> exposes the API beyond your machine. Set \u003Ccode>api_token\u003C/code> in the config first — see \u003Ca href=\"/docs/reference/api/\">HTTP API\u003C/a>.\u003C/p>\n\u003C/aside>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"query-commands\" aria-labelledby=\"heading-label-query-commands\">\u003Cspan id=\"heading-label-query-commands\">Query commands\u003C/span>\u003Ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#query-commands\" aria-label=\"Permalink to Query commands\" data-pagefind-ignore>\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\">#\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>All query commands read the local JSONL store under \u003Ccode>~/.nullwatch/data\u003C/code>; the server does not need to be running.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cfigure class=\"code-figure\" data-lang=\"bash\">\u003Cpre class=\"shiki null-kitchen\" style=\"background-color:#0a0806;color:#d9d1c3\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#ECE5D8\">zig\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> build\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> summary\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#ECE5D8\">zig\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> build\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> runs\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --verdict\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> pass\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --limit\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#D9A441\"> 20\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#ECE5D8\">zig\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> build\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> spans\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --source\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> nullclaw\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --tool-name\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> shell\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --limit\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#D9A441\"> 50\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#ECE5D8\">zig\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> build\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> evals\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --dataset\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> prod-shadow\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --verdict\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> fail\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#ECE5D8\">zig\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> build\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> run-123\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\u003Cbutton class=\"code-copy\" type=\"button\" data-code data-pagefind-ignore aria-live=\"polite\">copy\u003C/button>\u003C/figure>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Data table: Command, Flags\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ctable>\n\u003Cthead>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Cth>Command\u003C/th>\n\u003Cth>Flags\u003C/th>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003C/thead>\n\u003Ctbody>\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>runs\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>--run-id\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>--source\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>--operation\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>--status\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>--model\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>--tool-name\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>--verdict\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>--dataset\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>--limit\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>spans\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>--run-id\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>--trace-id\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>--source\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>--operation\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>--status\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>--model\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>--tool-name\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>--task-id\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>--session-id\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>--agent-id\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>--limit\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>evals\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>--run-id\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>--verdict\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>--eval-key\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>--scorer\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>--dataset\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>--limit\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003C/tbody>\n\u003C/table>\n\u003C/div>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"ingest-commands\" aria-labelledby=\"heading-label-ingest-commands\">\u003Cspan id=\"heading-label-ingest-commands\">Ingest commands\u003C/span>\u003Ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#ingest-commands\" aria-label=\"Permalink to Ingest commands\" data-pagefind-ignore>\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\">#\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>Both take a single JSON document via \u003Ccode>--json\u003C/code>. Field meanings are in the \u003Ca href=\"/docs/reference/api/\">data model\u003C/a>.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cfigure class=\"code-figure\" data-lang=\"bash\">\u003Cpre class=\"shiki null-kitchen\" style=\"background-color:#0a0806;color:#d9d1c3\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#ECE5D8\">zig\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> build\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> ingest-span\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --json\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> '{\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  \"run_id\": \"run-123\",\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  \"trace_id\": \"trace-123\",\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  \"span_id\": \"span-1\",\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  \"source\": \"nullclaw\",\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  \"operation\": \"model.call\",\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  \"status\": \"ok\",\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  \"started_at_ms\": 1710000000000,\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  \"ended_at_ms\": 1710000000320,\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  \"model\": \"gpt-5\",\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  \"prompt_version\": \"reply-v3\",\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  \"input_tokens\": 420,\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  \"output_tokens\": 96,\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  \"cost_usd\": 0.018\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">}'\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\u003Cbutton class=\"code-copy\" type=\"button\" data-code data-pagefind-ignore aria-live=\"polite\">copy\u003C/button>\u003C/figure>\n\u003Cfigure class=\"code-figure\" data-lang=\"bash\">\u003Cpre class=\"shiki null-kitchen\" style=\"background-color:#0a0806;color:#d9d1c3\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#ECE5D8\">zig\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> build\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> ingest-eval\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --json\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> '{\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  \"run_id\": \"run-123\",\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  \"eval_key\": \"helpfulness\",\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  \"scorer\": \"llm-judge\",\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  \"score\": 0.94,\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  \"verdict\": \"pass\",\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  \"dataset\": \"prod-shadow\"\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">}'\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\u003Cbutton class=\"code-copy\" type=\"button\" data-code data-pagefind-ignore aria-live=\"polite\">copy\u003C/button>\u003C/figure>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"demo-seed\" aria-labelledby=\"heading-label-demo-seed\">\u003Cspan id=\"heading-label-demo-seed\">demo-seed\u003C/span>\u003Ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#demo-seed\" aria-label=\"Permalink to demo-seed\" data-pagefind-ignore>\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\">#\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cfigure class=\"code-figure\" data-lang=\"bash\">\u003Cpre class=\"shiki null-kitchen\" style=\"background-color:#0a0806;color:#d9d1c3\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#ECE5D8\">zig\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> build\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> demo-seed\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\u003Cbutton class=\"code-copy\" type=\"button\" data-code data-pagefind-ignore aria-live=\"polite\">copy\u003C/button>\u003C/figure>\n\u003Cp>Creates a deterministic demo dataset of 3 runs (11 spans, 3 evals): a passing code-review run, a failed tool-call run, and a handoff/retry run with checkpoint context. No API keys, no hosted services, no agent workload. Seeding is idempotent — a second run skips all three existing run ids (\u003Ccode>runs_skipped: 3\u003C/code>) and creates nothing. Useful for demos, manual testing, and trying the \u003Ca href=\"https://hub.nullmenu.ai/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" aria-label=\"NullHub (opens in a new tab)\">NullHub\u003Csvg class=\"functional-icon external-icon\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\">\u003Cg stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.75\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">\u003Cpath d=\"M8 16 16 8\">\u003C/path>\u003Cpath d=\"M10 8h6v6\">\u003C/path>\u003C/g>\u003C/svg>\u003C/a> Observability page against real-shaped data:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cfigure class=\"code-figure\" data-lang=\"bash\">\u003Cpre class=\"shiki null-kitchen\" style=\"background-color:#0a0806;color:#d9d1c3\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#ECE5D8\">zig\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> build\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> demo-seed\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#ECE5D8\">zig\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> build\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> runs\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --limit\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#D9A441\"> 20\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#ECE5D8\">zig\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> build\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> demo-tool-failure\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\u003Cbutton class=\"code-copy\" type=\"button\" data-code data-pagefind-ignore aria-live=\"polite\">copy\u003C/button>\u003C/figure>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"nullhub-integration-flags\" aria-labelledby=\"heading-label-nullhub-integration-flags\">\u003Cspan id=\"heading-label-nullhub-integration-flags\">NullHub integration flags\u003C/span>\u003Ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#nullhub-integration-flags\" aria-label=\"Permalink to NullHub integration flags\" data-pagefind-ignore>\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\">#\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>NullWatch stays headless; these two flags let NullHub own installation and setup. Each must be the first argument — they are commands, not modifiers. \u003Ccode>--export-manifest\u003C/code> prints a JSON manifest with platform assets, ports and a 4-step setup-wizard schema; \u003Ccode>--from-json\u003C/code> writes \u003Ccode>~/.nullwatch/config.json\u003C/code> from the wizard&#39;s answers:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cfigure class=\"code-figure\" data-lang=\"bash\">\u003Cpre class=\"shiki null-kitchen\" style=\"background-color:#0a0806;color:#d9d1c3\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#877E6F;font-style:italic\"># print the nullhub manifest describing this component\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#ECE5D8\">zig\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> build\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --export-manifest\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#877E6F;font-style:italic\"># write config from wizard answers\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#ECE5D8\">zig\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> build\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --from-json\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> '{\"home\":\"~/.nullwatch\",\"port\":7710,\"data_dir\":\"data\"}'\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\u003Cbutton class=\"code-copy\" type=\"button\" data-code data-pagefind-ignore aria-live=\"polite\">copy\u003C/button>\u003C/figure>\n\u003Cp>The \u003Ccode>--from-json\u003C/code> payload also accepts \u003Ccode>host\u003C/code> and \u003Ccode>api_token\u003C/code>, matching the config file fields.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"environment\" aria-labelledby=\"heading-label-environment\">\u003Cspan id=\"heading-label-environment\">Environment\u003C/span>\u003Ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#environment\" aria-label=\"Permalink to Environment\" data-pagefind-ignore>\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\">#\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Data table: Variable, Used by, Meaning\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ctable>\n\u003Cthead>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Cth>Variable\u003C/th>\n\u003Cth>Used by\u003C/th>\n\u003Cth>Meaning\u003C/th>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003C/thead>\n\u003Ctbody>\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>NULLWATCH_HOME\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>nullwatch\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Alternate home directory instead of \u003Ccode>~/.nullwatch\u003C/code>; when unset, \u003Ccode>HOME\u003C/code> is used (\u003Ccode>USERPROFILE\u003C/code> on Windows)\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>NULLWATCH_URL\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>NullHub\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Where NullHub finds a running NullWatch, e.g. \u003Ccode>http://127.0.0.1:7710\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003C/tbody>\n\u003C/table>\n\u003C/div>\n",[13,16,19,21,24,27,29,32],{"id":14,"text":15,"depth":8},"commands","Commands",{"id":17,"text":18,"depth":8},"shared-flags","Shared flags",{"id":20,"text":20,"depth":8},"serve",{"id":22,"text":23,"depth":8},"query-commands","Query commands",{"id":25,"text":26,"depth":8},"ingest-commands","Ingest commands",{"id":28,"text":28,"depth":8},"demo-seed",{"id":30,"text":31,"depth":8},"nullhub-integration-flags","NullHub integration flags",{"id":33,"text":34,"depth":8},"environment","Environment","2026-07-17","Reference",{"siteId":2,"section":3,"slug":38,"path":39,"title":40,"description":41,"order":42,"verified":9,"sectionTitle":36},"api","/content/watch/docs/reference/api.md","HTTP API","Endpoints, data model, query parameters and token auth for the NullWatch JSON API.",1,null],"uses":{"params":["section","slug"]}}]}
